linux/scripts/tests/test-riscv64-isa-gate.sh	docs/riscv64-rva23-baseline.md

# (b) Pointers into refactoring-backlog.md. These must NOT be anchored: an OPEN
# backlog entry is archived when it closes, so an anchor there is built to rot, and
# the gate exempts archives from the anchor check precisely because dated records
# must not be edited to keep a gate quiet. The fix is to re-point each of these at
# the durable page that explains the behaviour -- per file, not mechanical.
linux/scripts/tests/test-codec-so-map-convergence.sh	docs/refactoring-backlog.md
